  "Date": "2026-05-06T18:07:31Z",
  "Message": "docs(plans): 18k rps DB stress lab implementation plan\n\nMaps the spec into 8 phases with bite-sized tasks:\n0. Branch setup in perfana-demo\n1. postgres + pgbouncer config files\n2. Lab compose stack + drivers compose\n3. Java driver (8 tasks): build, UrlPatternLoader, RecordFactory + tests,\n   DriverConfig + SamplePump, MetricsLogger, SyntheticDriver, Dockerfile\n4. Bash scripts (10 tasks): common.sh, preflight, mint-api-key, seed,\n   verify-chunks, observability, poll-perf-analysis, trigger-refetch,\n   snapshot/restore, run-soak orchestrator\n5. Python report generator + SLO evaluation\n6. README\n7. Smoke (5-min Stage 1)\n8. Real Stage 1, Stage 2, Stage 3 + SUMMARY\n\nEach task has checkboxed steps with full code or precise content\ndescriptions, exact commands, and expected output. Six implementer-note\ncall-outs flag specific files/line-numbers that must be cross-checked\nbefore code compiles (TimescaleDBWriter field names, TimescaleDBConfig,\nKeycloak realm, test-runs DTO, chunk-id path, analyzeTest envelope).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
